pwd - To check the current directory
ls - To list all the things in the current directory
cd - To change the directory(if we just type in the first unique letters and press tab it will automatically types it inn)
cd .. - To up a directory
cd ../.. - To up two directories at a time
cd / - To go to home directory
mkdir - To make a directory
touch - To make a file
ls -l - We get things like permissions, owner, size, and date(-l for long format)
ls - a - Shows all the hidden files(-a for all)
ls - la - Lists everything, including hidden files, in long format(-la is essentially -l and -a)
ls -r - Lists in reverse order(ls --reverse)
cat - To access the data in a txt file

whoami - It gives the name of the user/device
nano - To update the file contains
whatis - To know what a command is
which - To know where the command is
explorer.exe - To open an image/png file
